$DIR/main.p:15:11: p holds a view of s (s.a.New[int](), line 12), which was reclaimed by s.a.Reset() at line 14, so p can no longer be used here
    p looks at memory that s owns, without owning it: the view was made by
    s.a.New[int]() at line 12. A view of a local arena's memory may be used only
    until Reset or Release reclaims it. At line 14 s was reclaimed by
    s.a.Reset(), so the view may look at memory that was released, or at a value
    that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use p before line 14, or call s.a.Reset() only after the last use of p
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)
